  "notes": "Single-cell characterization data for NCA Samsung INR21700-50E and NMC LG-Chem INR21700-M50T cells, and parallel-connected module experiments. The README warns modules are not single cells. Two cell models are used in the modules (Samsung INR21700-50E, NCA, and LG-Chem INR21700-M50T, NMC), per the landing page. Both are ~5 Ah-class 21700 cells with matching 2.5-4.2V limits; recorded values are for the Samsung cell specifically (official datasheet), with LG M50T's nearly identical spec (18.2Wh/3.63V nominal = ~5.0Ah, 2.5-4.2V, dia<=21.10mm x height<=70.15mm, from LG's INR21700 M50 18.2Wh spec, the closest available document to the exact M50T tab variant) noted here rather than forced into these singular fields. Charging profile: the conditions vary temperature, interconnection resistance, chemistry and ageing, not the charge rate. The registry says MultiC; all 54 module experiments charge at 6.5 A and discharge at 14.6 A, and the single-cell files are pseudo-OCV and HPPC multisine, so no varying C-rate was found. Unresolved. The data article (Piombo et al., Data in Brief 53 (2024) 110227; full text read) states: 39 single cells (19 new LG Chem INR21700-M50T NMC with codes P1-P20, 18 new Samsung INR21700-50E NCA with codes F1-F18, one pre-aged cell per chemistry, GS3 for NCA and Y1 for NMC) with Silicon-doped graphite negative electrodes, characterised at 23 C (C/20 pseudo-OCV, HPPC, MultiSine), and 54 module-level experiments on two twin test benches (M1, M2), four cells in parallel in a ladder configuration, in a full factorial design: temperature 10, 25 and 40 C, interconnection resistance 0, 1 and 3 mOhm, chemistry NMC, NCA or mixed (two NMC and two NCA), aged or unaged. Module test: C/3 CC-CV charge to 4.2 V (CV to 200 mA), 0.75C CC discharge to 2.5 V, 1 s sampling, Arbin LBT22013 and an Amerex IC500R chamber, T-type thermocouples at the centre of each cell (surface temperature) and Honeywell SS495A Hall sensors for the branch currents; the module C-rates refer to the four-cell capacity (C/3 is the 6.5 A and 0.75C the 14.6 A seen in the data). Per-single-cell capacities are the paper's Table 1 values (Samsung 4.90 Ah, LG 4.85 Ah); the dataset-level capacity is null because the two differ, and the module entities carry none. Table 1 gives the nominal voltage 3.63 V and the diameter 21.44 mm only for the LG cell, the Samsung diameter being 21.25 mm; the recorded 21.25 x 70.8 mm dimensions are the Samsung ones. The related analysis paper is Piombo et al., Journal of Energy Storage 84 (2024) 110783, 10.1016/j.est.2024.110783. Rate groups: the C/3 CC-CV charge against the HPPC pulses, whose current levels are not stated."
